{"id": "commentary:Metzudat-David:judg-5-22:seg1", "corpus_id": "traditional-commentaries", "work": "Metzudat David on Judges", "locator": "5:22:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Metzudat_David_on_Judges?context=0&pad=0", "edition": "Sefaria default Hebrew book response; available version metadata: On Your Way", "language": "he", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": "tanakh-wlc-judg-5-22", "quote": "אז הלמו וגו׳. רצה לומר, כי בראותם הנחל שוטף, נסו לנפשם על הסוסים, ואז הוכו ונשברו עקבי הסוס מן הדהרות ודליגות שעשו עמהם אנשיו הגבורים רוכבי הסוסים, או מלת ׳אביריו׳ חוזר על הסוסים, ורצה לומר, מן הדהרות שעשו סוסיו החזקים:", "context": "Entire verse commentary cell read. Exact segment 1 after HTML removal; explicit index title Metzudat David on Judges. Index URL https://www.sefaria.org/api/index/Metzudat_David_on_Judges", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Flight from the flooding river and forceful galloping break horses heels; alternatively the strong ones are the horses themselves.", "epistemic_type": "traditional_commentary", "reviewers": ["COM-003 worker"], "task_id": "COM-003", "limitations": ["Default API Hebrew response may combine available digital versions; metadata list does not identify a collated print witness.", "No independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
