{"id": "commentary:Rashi:1kgs-10-28:seg2", "corpus_id": "traditional-commentaries", "work": "Rashi on I Kings", "locator": "10:28:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Rashi_on_I_Kings?context=0&pad=0", "edition": "Sefaria default Hebrew book response; available version metadata: The Metsudah Tanach series, Lakewood, N.J  | On Your Way -- new", "language": "he", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": "tanakh-wlc-1kgs-10-28", "quote": "וּמִקְוֵה. אֲסֵפַת סוֹחֲרֵי הַסּוּסִים בְּמִצְרַיִם, סוֹחֲרֵי הַמֶּלֶךְ שְׁלֹמֹה הָיוּ קוֹנִין אוֹתָם בִּמְחִיר מִמִּצְרַיִם מִן הַמֶּלֶךְ, שֶׁלֹּא יוֹצִיא אָדָם סוּס מִשָּׁם, אֶלָּא עַל יָדָם, כָּךְ שָׁמַעְתִּי. וּלְכָךְ נָקוּד עַל 'וּמִקְוֵה' טַעַם זָקֵ\"ף גָּדוֹל, לִלְמֹד שֶׁהַתֵּבָה עוֹמֶדֶת בְּעַצְמָהּ, וְאֵינָהּ דְּבוּקָה לְאַחֲרֶיהָ.", "context": "Entire verse commentary cell read. Exact segment 2 after HTML removal; explicit index title Rashi on I Kings. Index URL https://www.sefaria.org/api/index/Rashi_on_I_Kings", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Reports an Egyptian horse trade controlled by Solomon’s merchants; explicitly marks the explanation as something heard, not independently established economic history.", "epistemic_type": "traditional_commentary", "reviewers": ["COM-003 worker"], "task_id": "COM-003", "limitations": ["Default API Hebrew response may combine available digital versions; metadata list does not identify a collated print witness.", "No independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
