{"id": "commentary:Rashi:2kgs-23-11:seg1", "corpus_id": "traditional-commentaries", "work": "Rashi on II Kings", "locator": "23:11:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Rashi_on_II_Kings?context=0&pad=0", "edition": "Sefaria default Hebrew book response; available version metadata: The Metsudah Tanach series, Lakewood, N.J | On Your Way -- new", "language": "he", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": "tanakh-wlc-2kgs-23-11", "quote": "אֶת הַסּוּסִים. אוֹתָם הַמִּשְׁתַּחֲוִים לַחַמָּה, הָיוּ לָהֶם סוּסִים מוּכָנִים לָצֵאת לִקְרַאת הַחַמָּה בַּבֹּקֶר.", "context": "Entire verse commentary cell read. Exact segment 1 after HTML removal; explicit index title Rashi on II Kings. Index URL https://www.sefaria.org/api/index/Rashi_on_II_Kings", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": true}, "interpretation": "Horses were prepared to meet the sun each morning by sun worshippers; solar ritual association, not stated celestial travel.", "epistemic_type": "traditional_commentary", "reviewers": ["COM-003 worker", "/root/core_verify_finish (independent of COM-003 author)"], "task_id": "COM-003", "limitations": ["Default API Hebrew response may combine available digital versions; metadata list does not identify a collated print witness.", "No independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}, "verification_notes": ["All three verse comments read. Sun worshippers prepare horses to go out to meet the sun in the morning. Solar cult association and ordinary horses are explicit; no celestial solar-horse species or cosmic journey is asserted. Keep separate from a proven history of cultural borrowing."]}
