{"id": "commentary:Metzudat-David:isa-66-20:seg1", "corpus_id": "traditional-commentaries", "work": "Metzudat David on Isaiah", "locator": "66:20:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Metzudat_David_on_Isaiah?context=0&pad=0", "edition": "Sefaria default Hebrew book response; available version metadata: On Your Way", "language": "he", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": "tanakh-wlc-isa-66-20", "quote": "והביאו את כל אחיכם. בני ישראל הרחוקים שלא עלו עם אחיהם אותם העכו״ם שישראל הם בתוכם כשישמעו הפלא הגדול שיעשה המקום במחנה גוג ומגוג יביאו את ישראל בסוסים וברכב וכו׳ למנחה לה׳: ", "context": "Entire verse commentary cell read. Exact segment 1 after HTML removal; explicit index title Metzudat David on Isaiah. Index URL https://www.sefaria.org/api/index/Metzudat_David_on_Isaiah", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Foreign nations bring dispersed Israelites by ordinary mounts and vehicles after the Gog and Magog event; transport destination is Jerusalem, not another world.", "epistemic_type": "traditional_commentary", "reviewers": ["COM-003 worker"], "task_id": "COM-003", "limitations": ["Default API Hebrew response may combine available digital versions; metadata list does not identify a collated print witness.", "No independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"id": "commentary:Rashi:jer-12-5:seg2", "corpus_id": "traditional-commentaries", "work": "Rashi on Jeremiah", "locator": "12:5:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Rashi_on_Jeremiah?context=0&pad=0", "edition": "Sefaria default Hebrew book response; available version metadata: Sefaria vocalized edition | On Your Way", "language": "he", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": "tanakh-wlc-jer-12-5", "quote": "וְאֵיךְ תְּתַחֲרֶה אֶת הַסּוּסִים. לָרוּץ אֶת הַסּוּסִים; כְּלוֹמַר: וּמָה קְרוֹבֶיךָ הַכֹּהֲנִים בָּאִים לְהָרְגְךָ, כָּל שֶׁכֵּן שֶׁיָּקוּמוּ לְהוֹרְגְךָ שָׂרֵי יְהוּדָה; וְזֶהוּ קִצְפִּי עֲלֵיהֶם, וְזוֹ הִיא הַצְלָחַת הָאוֹיֵב. וְכֵן תִּרְגֵּם יוֹנָתָן: ״דְּנָא תְּיוּבְתָּא וְגוֹ׳״. וּמִדְרַשׁ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ (סנהדרין צו.): אִם עַל שְׂכַר שָׁלֹשׁ פְּסִיעוֹת שֶׁרָץ נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּר לִכְבוֹדִי בִּימֵי מְרֹדַךְ בַּלְאֲדָן אַתָּה תָּמֵהַּ, שֶׁהִרְבֵּיתִי גְדֻלָּתוֹ כָּל כָּךְ, מָה תִּתְמַהּ עוֹד כְּשֶׁתִּרְאֶה שִׁלּוּם שָׂכָר שֶׁאֲשַׁלֵּם לַצַּדִּיקִים שֶׁרָצוּ לְפָנַי כַּסּוּסִים!", "context": "Entire verse commentary cell read. Exact segment 2 after HTML removal; explicit index title Rashi on Jeremiah. Index URL https://www.sefaria.org/api/index/Rashi_on_Jeremiah", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Preserves two readings: threatening Judah’s leaders beyond local priests; rabbinic comparison of Nebuchadnezzar’s few steps and reward to righteous people running like horses. No literal spirit mount.", "epistemic_type": "traditional_commentary", "reviewers": ["COM-003 worker"], "task_id": "COM-003", "limitations": ["Default API Hebrew response may combine available digital versions; metadata list does not identify a collated print witness.", "No independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independen