n": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-96a-5-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "96a:5", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.96a.5", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.96a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "״וַיִּרְדֹּף עַד דָּן״. אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: כֵּיוָן שֶׁבָּא אוֹתוֹ צַדִּיק עַד דָּן, תָּשַׁשׁ כֹּחוֹ. רָאָה בְּנֵי בָּנָיו שֶׁעֲתִידִין לַעֲבוֹד עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה בְּדָן, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״וַיָּשֶׂם אֶת הָאֶחָד בְּבֵית אֵל וְאֶת הָאֶחָד נָתַן בְּדָן״. וְאַף אוֹתוֹ רָשָׁע לֹא נִתְגַּבֵּר עַד שֶׁהִגִּיעַ לְדָן, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״מִדָּן נִשְׁמַע נַחְרַת סוּסָיו״.", "context": "Read 96a:4–10. R. Yohanan interprets Abraham’s weakness at Dan through future idolatry, then enemy strengthening there supported by Jeremiah’s horse-snorting quotation. Military horse sound; surrounding angelic assistance does not transform horse species.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 96a:4–10. R. Yohanan interprets Abraham’s weakness at Dan through future idolatry, then enemy strengthening there supported by Jeremiah’s horse-snorting quotation. Military horse sound; surrounding angelic assistance does not transform horse species.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["aggadah", "enemy_horses_biblical_exegesis"], "role": "enemy_horses_biblical_exegesis", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-96a-7-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "96a:7", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.96a.7", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.96a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "״צַדִּיק אַתָּה ה׳ כִּי אָרִיב אֵלֶיךָ אַךְ מִשְׁפָּטִים אֲדַבֵּר אוֹתָךְ מַדּוּעַ דֶּרֶךְ רְשָׁעִים צָלֵחָה שָׁלוּ כׇּל בֹּגְדֵי בָגֶד. נְטַעְתָּם גַּם שֹׁרָשׁוּ יֵלְכוּ גַּם עָשׂוּ פֶרִי״. מַאי אַהְדַּרוּ לֵיהּ? ״כִּי אֶת רַגְלִים רַצְתָּה וַיַּלְאוּךָ וְאֵיךְ תְּתַחֲרֶה אֶת הַסּוּסִים וּבְאֶרֶץ שָׁלוֹם אַתָּה בוֹטֵחַ וְאֵיךְ תַּעֲשֶׂה בִּגְאוֹן הַיַּרְדֵּן״.", "context": "Read 96a:4–10. Jeremiah’s question about wicked prosperity receives running against footmen/horses verse; following parable and patriarchs comparison explain divine reward. Figurative theological use of horse speed.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 96a:4–10. Jeremiah’s question about wicked prosperity receives running against footmen/horses verse; following parable and patriarchs comparison explain divine reward. Figurative theological use of horse speed.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["aggadah", "running_horse_scriptural_simile"], "role": "running_horse_scriptural_simile", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-96a-8-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "96a:8", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.96a.8", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.96a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מָשָׁל לְאָדָם אֶחָד שֶׁאָמַר: יָכוֹל אֲנִי לָרוּץ שָׁלֹשׁ פַּרְסָאוֹת לִפְנֵי הַסּוּסִים בֵּין בִּצְעֵי הַמַּיִם. נִזְדַּמֵּן לוֹ רַגְלִי אֶחָד, רָץ לְפָנָיו שְׁלֹשָׁה מִילִין בַּיַּבָּשָׁה וְנִלְאָה. אָמְרוּ לוֹ: וּמָה לִפְנֵי רַגְלִי כָּךְ, לִפְנֵי הַסּוּסִים – עַל אַחַת כַּמָּה וְכַמָּה. וּמָה שְׁלֹשֶׁת מִילִין כָּךְ, שָׁלֹשׁ פַּרְסָאוֹת – עַל אַחַת כַּמָּה וְכַמָּה. וּמָה בַּיַּבָּשָׁה כָּךְ, בֵּין בִּצְעֵי הַמַּיִם – עַל אַחַת כַּמָּה וְכַמָּה.", "context": "Read 96a:7–10. Explicit parable contrasts tired runner against pedestrian versus horses, distances and terrain; applied to reward in next segment. Ordinary horse capacities provide rhetorical comparison, not spirit animals.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 96a:7–10. Explicit parable contrasts tired runner against pedestrian versus horses, distances and terrain; applied to reward in next segment. Ordinary horse capacities provide rhetorical comparison, not spirit animals.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["aggadah", "horse_racing_reward_parable"], "role": "horse_racing_reward_parable", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-96a-9-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "96a:9", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.96a.9", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.96a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אַף אַתָּה: וּמָה בִּשְׂכַר אַרְבַּע פְּסִיעוֹת שֶׁשִּׁלַּמְתִּי לְאוֹתוֹ רָשָׁע, שֶׁרָץ אַחַר כְּבוֹדִי, אַתָּה תָּמֵיהַּ? כְּשֶׁאֲנִי מְשַׁלֵּם שָׂכָר לְאַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב שֶׁרָצוּ לְפָנַי כְּסוּסִים – עַל אַחַת כַּמָּה וְכַמָּה! הַיְינוּ דִּכְתִיב: ״לַנְּבִאִים נִשְׁבַּר לִבִּי בְקִרְבִּי רָחֲפוּ כׇּל עַצְמֹתַי הָיִיתִי כְּאִישׁ שִׁכּוֹר וּכְגֶבֶר עֲבָרוֹ יָיִן מִפְּנֵי ה׳ וּמִפְּנֵי דִּבְרֵי קׇדְשׁוֹ״.", "context": "Read 96a:7–10. God’s represented answer contrasts reward for wicked man’s four steps with patriarchs running before Him like horses. Explicit simile, not patriarchs becoming literal horses or heavenly mounts.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 96a:7–10. God’s represented answer contrasts reward for wicked man’s four steps with patriarchs running before Him like horses. Explicit simile, not patriarchs becoming literal horses or heavenly mounts.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["aggadah", "patriarchs_horses_reward_simile"], "role": "patriarchs_horses_reward_simile", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-51b-7-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "51b:7", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.51b.7", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Shabbat.51b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַתְנִי׳ בַּמֶּה בְּהֵמָה יוֹצְאָה וּבַמָּה אֵינָהּ יוֹצְאָה? — יוֹצֵא הַגָּמָל בְּאַפְסָר, וְנָאֲקָה בַּחֲטָם, וְלוּבְדְּקִים בִּפְרוּמְבְּיָא, וְסוּס בְּשֵׁיר.", "context": "Read 51b:7–18 and 52a:1–7. Embedded Mishnah permits horse to go out with shir restraint; following discussion distinguishes species and needed/excess restraint. Ordinary animal equipment.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 51b:7–18 and 52a:1–7. Embedded Mishnah permits horse to go out with shir restraint; following discussion distinguishes species and needed/excess restraint. Ordinary animal equipment.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["halakha", "sabbath_horse_restraint"], "role": "sabbath_horse_restraint", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-51b-14-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "51b:14", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.51b.14", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Shabbat.51b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר לְפָנָיו רַבִּי יִשְׁמָעֵאל בְּרַבִּי יוֹסֵי: כָּךְ אָמַר אַבָּא: אַרְבַּע בְּהֵמוֹת יוֹצְאוֹת בְּאַפְסָר, הַסּוּס וְהַפֶּרֶד וְהַגָּמָל וְהַחֲמוֹר. לְמַעוֹטֵי מַאי? לַָאו לְמַעוֹטֵי גָּמָל בַּחֲטָם! לָא, לְמַעוֹטֵי נָאקָה בְּאַפְסָר.", "context": "Read 51b:7–18 and 52a:1–7. R. Ishmael b. R. Yose reports his father’s four animals permitted in halter: horse, mule, camel, donkey; debate asks which excessive restraint excluded. Mule kept distinct.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 51b:7–18 and 52a:1–7. R. Ishmael b. R. Yose reports his father’s four animals permitted in halter: horse, mule, camel, donkey; debate asks which excessive restraint excluded. Mule kept distinct.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["halakha", "sabbath_halter_species"], "role": "sabbath_halter_species", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "boundary_species": "mule explicitly separate from horse", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-52a-5-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "52a:5", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.52a.5", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Shabbat.52a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אֲמַר לֵיהּ אַבָּיֵי: אַדְּרַבָּה, תִּסְתַּיֵּים דִּשְׁמוּאֵל הוּא דְּאָמַר בֵּין לְנוֹי בֵּין לְשַׁמֵּר — אָסוּר. דְּאָמַר רַב יְהוּדָה אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: מַחְלִיפִין לִפְנֵי רַבִּי, שֶׁל זוֹ בְּזוֹ מַהוּ? אָמַר לְפָנָיו רַבִּי יִשְׁמָעֵאל בְּרַבִּי יוֹסֵי, כָּךְ אָמַר אַבָּא: אַרְבַּע בְּהֵמוֹת יוֹצְאוֹת בְּאַפְסָר — הַסּוּס הַפֶּרֶד וְהַגָּמָל וְהַחֲמוֹר. לָאו לְמַעוֹטֵי גָּמָל בַּחֲטָם? סָמִי הָא מִקַּמֵּי הָא.", "context": "Read 51b:7–18 and 52a:1–7. Abaye challenges attribution of restraint view using four-animal halter report. Distinct canonical repetition of 51b:14, not a second independent rule.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 51b:7–18 and 52a:1–7. Abaye challenges attribution of restraint view using four-animal halter report. Distinct canonical repetition of 51b:14, not a second independent rule.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["halakha", "sabbath_halter_species_argument"], "role": "sabbath_halter_species_argument", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "boundary_species": "mule explicitly separate from horse", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-53a-12-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "53a:12", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.53a.12", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Shabbat.53a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מֵיתִיבִי: לֹא יֵצֵא הַסּוּס בִּזְנַב שׁוּעָל, וְלֹא בַּזַּהֲרוּרִית שֶׁבֵּין עֵינָיו. לֹא יֵצֵא הַזָּב בַּכִּיס שֶׁלּוֹ, וְלֹא עִזִּים בַּכִּיס שֶׁבְּדַדֵּיהֶן, וְלֹא פָּרָה בַּחִסּוּם שֶׁבְּפִיהָ, וְלֹא סְיָיחִים בַּטְּרַסְקָלִין שֶׁבְּפִיהֶם לִרְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים, וְלֹא בְּהֵמָה בַּסַּנְדָּל שֶׁבְּרַגְלֶיהָ, וְלֹא בַּקָּמֵיעַ אַף עַל פִּי שֶׁהוּא מוּמְחֶה — וְזֶה חוֹמֶר בַּבְּהֵמָה מִבָּאָדָם.", "context": "Read 53a:10–15. Baraita prohibits horse fox-tail/bright forehead equipment among list of animal outings, including prohibition of animal amulet even expert one; succeeding list permits wound/fracture dressings. Broad animal amulet clause not proof the horse itself is magical; purpose of specific fox-tail ornament not settled without commentary.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Read 53a:10–15. Baraita prohibits horse fox-tail/bright forehead equipment among list of animal outings, including prohibition of animal amulet even expert one; succeeding list permits wound/fracture dressings. Broad animal amulet clause not proof the horse itself is magical; purpose of specific fox-tail ornament not settled without commentary.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-003", "categories": ["halakha", "sabbath_horse_equipment_amulet_boundary"], "role": "sabbath_horse_equipment_amulet_boundary", "limitations": ["Digital edition/API segmentation checked; no manuscript or traditional commentary collation.", "Not independently reviewed; adjacent miracles do not establish extraordinary horse status."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-pesachim-3b-14-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Pesachim", "locator": "3b:14", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim.3b.14", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Pesachim.3b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "יוֹחָנָן חָקוֹקָאָה נְפַק לְקִרְיָיתָא. כִּי אֲתָא, אֲמַרוּ לֵיהּ: חִיטִּין נַעֲשׂוּ יָפוֹת? אָמַר לָהֶם: שְׂעוֹרִים נַעֲשׂוּ יָפוֹת. אֲמַרוּ לֵיהּ: צֵא וּבַשֵּׂר לַסּוּסִים וְלַחֲמוֹרִים, דִּכְתִיב: ״הַשְּׂעֹרִים וְהַתֶּבֶן לַסּוּסִים וְלָרָכֶשׁ״. מַאי הֲוֵי לֵיהּ לְמֵימַר? אֶשְׁתָּקַד נַעֲשׂוּ חִיטִּין יָפוֹת. אִי נָמֵי: עֲדָשִׁים נַעֲשׂוּ יָפוֹת.", "context": "Read segments 12,13,14 of Pesachim 3b. Yohanan reports good barley instead of wheat; interlocutors sarcastically tell him to announce this to horses and donkeys, citing royal fodder provisions. Rhetoric about tactful speech.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Yohanan reports good barley instead of wheat; interlocutors sarcastically tell him to announce this to horses and donkeys, citing royal fodder provisions. Rhetoric about tactful speech.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "fodder_rhetoric", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-46a-12-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "46a:12", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.46a.12", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.46a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "וּמַעֲשֶׂה בְּאֶחָד שֶׁרָכַב עַל סוּס בְּשַׁבָּת בִּימֵי יְוָנִים, וֶהֱבִיאוּהוּ לְבֵית דִּין וּסְקָלוּהוּ, לֹא מִפְּנֵי שֶׁרָאוּי לְכָךְ, אֶלָּא שֶׁהַשָּׁעָה צְרִיכָה לְכָךְ. שׁוּב מַעֲשֶׂה בְּאָדָם אֶחָד שֶׁהֵטִיחַ אֶת אִשְׁתּוֹ תַּחַת הַתְּאֵנָה, וֶהֱבִיאוּהוּ לְבֵית דִּין וְהִלְקוּהוּ, לֹא מִפְּנֵי שֶׁרָאוּי לְכָךְ, אֶלָּא שֶׁהַשָּׁעָה צְרִיכָה לְכָךְ.", "context": "Read segments 10,11,12,13,14 of Sanhedrin 46a. R. Eliezer ben Jacob’s account of emergency judicial punishment: Sabbath horse rider stoned in Greek times, explicitly because the hour required it rather than normal deserved penalty.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Eliezer ben Jacob’s account of emergency judicial punishment: Sabbath horse rider stoned in Greek times, explicitly because the hour required it rather than normal deserved penalty.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "emergency_sabbath_punishment", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-avodah-zarah-11a-13-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Avodah Zarah", "locator": "11a:13", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah.11a.13", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Avodah_Zarah.11a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "וּמִידֵּי אַחֲרִינָא לָא? וְהָתַנְיָא: עוֹקְרִין עַל הַמְּלָכִים, וְאֵין בּוֹ מִשּׁוּם דַּרְכֵי הָאֱמוֹרִי! אָמַר רַב פָּפָּא: סוּס שֶׁרָכַב עָלָיו.", "context": "Read segments 11,12,13,14 of Avodah Zarah 11a. Rav Pappa limits royal funeral animal hamstringing to the horse the king rode; discussion concerns funeral honor and forbidden gentile custom.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Rav Pappa limits royal funeral animal hamstringing to the horse the king rode; discussion concerns funeral honor and forbidden gentile custom.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "royal_funeral_hamstringing", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-avodah-zarah-13a-15-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Avodah Zarah", "locator": "13a:15", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah.13a.15", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Avodah_Zarah.13a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר מָר: בְּהֵמָה תֵּיעָקֵר. וְהָא אִיכָּא צַעַר בַּעֲלֵי חַיִּים! אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: אָמַר רַחֲמָנָא ״אֶת סוּסֵיהֶם תְּעַקֵּר״.", "context": "Read segments 13,14,15,16 of Avodah Zarah 13a. Abaye cites the command to hamstring enemy horses in response to animal suffering objection in discussion of animals acquired at an idolatrous fair. This is legal reasoning using Scripture.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Abaye cites the command to hamstring enemy horses in response to animal suffering objection in discussion of animals acquired at an idolatrous fair. This is legal reasoning using Scripture.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "hamstringing_scriptural_exception", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bava-kamma-18b-17-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bava Kamma", "locator": "18b:17", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma.18b.17", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bava_Kamma.18b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תָּא שְׁמַע, דְּתָנֵי רָמֵי בַּר יְחֶזְקֵאל: תַּרְנְגוֹל שֶׁהוֹשִׁיט רֹאשׁוֹ לַאֲוִיר כְּלִי זְכוּכִית, וְתָקַע בּוֹ וּשְׁבָרוֹ – מְשַׁלֵּם נֶזֶק שָׁלֵם. וְאָמַר רַב יוֹסֵף, אָמְרִי בֵּי רַב: סוּס שֶׁצָּנַף וַחֲמוֹר שֶׁנָּעַר, וְשִׁיבֵּר אֶת הַכֵּלִים – מְשַׁלֵּם חֲצִי נֶזֶק.", "context": "Read segments 15,16,17,18 of Bava Kamma 18b. Attributed school ruling: a neighing horse or braying donkey that breaks vessels incurs half damages; compared with rooster sound damage.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Attributed school ruling: a neighing horse or braying donkey that breaks vessels incurs half damages; compared with rooster sound damage.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "neighing_damage", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bava-metzia-58b-5-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bava Metzia", "locator": "58b:5", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia.58b.5", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bava_Metzia.58b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תַּנְיָא, רַבִּי יְהוּדָה בֶּן בְּתֵירָא אוֹמֵר: אַף הַמּוֹכֵר סוּס וְסַיִיף וַחֲטִיטוֹם בַּמִּלְחָמָה – אֵין לָהֶם אוֹנָאָה, מִפְּנֵי שֶׁיֵּשׁ בָּהֶן חַיֵּי נֶפֶשׁ.", "context": "Read segments 3,4,5,6,7 of Bava Metzia 58b. R. Judah ben Beteira exempts wartime horse, sword and shield sales from price fraud rules because life depends on them; attributed legal opinion.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Judah ben Beteira exempts wartime horse, sword and shield sales from price fraud rules because life depends on them; attributed legal opinion.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "wartime_price_exception", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-megillah-16a-6-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Megillah", "locator": "16a:6", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah.16a.6", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Megillah.16a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "״וַיִּקַּח הָמָן אֶת הַלְּבוּשׁ וְאֶת הַסּוּס״. אֲזַל אַשְׁכְּחֵיהּ דְּיָתְבִי רַבָּנַן קַמֵּיהּ וּמַחְוֵי לְהוּ הִלְכוֹת קְמִיצָה לְרַבָּנַן, כֵּיוָן דְּחַזְיֵיהּ מָרְדְּכַי דְּאַפֵּיק לְקִבְלֵיהּ וְסוּסְיָא מֵיחַד בִּידֵיהּ, מִירְתַת. אֲמַר לְהוּ לְרַבָּנַן: הַאי רַשִּׁיעָא לְמִיקְטַל נַפְשַׁי קָא אָתֵי זִילוּ מִקַּמֵּיהּ דִּי לָא תִּכָּווּ בְּגַחַלְתּוֹ. בְּהָהִיא שַׁעְתָּא נִתְעַטֵּף מָרְדְּכַי וְקָם לֵיהּ לִצְלוֹתָא, אֲתָא הָמָן וִיתֵיב לֵיהּ קַמַּיְיהוּ וְאוֹרֵיךְ עַד דְּסַלֵּיק מָרְדֳּכַי לִצְלוֹתֵיהּ.", "context": "Read segments 4,5,6,7,8 of Megillah 16a. Haman brings royal clothing and horse; Mordecai initially fears execution and prays while Haman waits. Esther narrative exposition.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Haman brings royal clothing and horse; Mordecai initially fears execution and prays while Haman waits. Esther narrative exposition.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "mordecai_royal_honor", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-megillah-16a-8-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Megillah", "locator": "16a:8", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah.16a.8", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Megillah.16a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אֲמַר לֵיהּ: קוּם לְבוֹשׁ הָנֵי מָאנֵי וּרְכוֹב הַאי סוּסְיָא, דְּבָעֵי לָךְ מַלְכָּא. אֲמַר לֵיהּ: לָא יָכֵילְנָא עַד דְּעָיֵילְנָא לְבֵי בָנֵי וְאֶשְׁקוֹל לְמַזְיָיא, דְּלָאו אוֹרַח אַרְעָא לְאִשְׁתַּמּוֹשֵׁי בְּמָאנֵי דְמַלְכָּא הָכִי.", "context": "Read segments 6,7,8,9,10 of Megillah 16a. Haman tells Mordecai to wear the clothes and ride the royal horse; Mordecai requests bathing and haircut before royal honor. Subsequent scene makes Haman his mount-up support.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Haman tells Mordecai to wear the clothes and ride the royal horse; Mordecai requests bathing and haircut before royal honor. Subsequent scene makes Haman his mount-up support.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "mordecai_royal_honor_preparation", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-shabbat-152a-6-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Shabbat", "locator": "152a:6", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat.152a.6", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Shabbat.152a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "חַזְיֵיהּ דְּלָא סָיֵים מְסָאנֵיהּ, אֲמַר לֵיהּ: דְּעַל סוּס — מֶלֶךְ, דְּעַל חֲמוֹר — בֶּן חוֹרִין, וּדְמַנְעָלֵי בְּרִיגְלוֹהִי — בַּר אִינִישׁ. דְּלָא הָא וְלָא הָא — דַּחֲפִיר וּקְבִיר טָב מִינֵּיהּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ: גּוֹזָא גּוֹזָא, תְּלָת אֲמַרְתְּ לִי, תְּלָת שָׁמְעַתְּ: הַדְרַת פָּנִים — זָקָן, שִׂמְחַת לֵב — אִשָּׁה, ״נַחֲלַת ה׳ — בָּנִים״. בָּרוּךְ הַמָּקוֹם שֶׁמְּנָעֲךָ מִכּוּלָּם. אֲמַר לֵיהּ: קָרְחָא מְצַוֵּי?! אֲמַר לֵיהּ: עִיקְרָא שְׁלִיפָא תּוֹכֵחָה!", "context": "Read segments 4,5,6,7,8 of Shabbat 152a. A eunuch tells R. Joshua ben Korha that horse riding marks a king, donkey riding a free person, shoes a human; polemical banter, not a formal social census.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A eunuch tells R. Joshua ben Korha that horse riding marks a king, donkey riding a free person, shoes a human; polemical banter, not a formal social census.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "riding_social_rank_proverb", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sotah-42a-10-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sotah", "locator": "42a:10", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah.42a.10", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sotah.42a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "״אַל יֵרַךְ לְבַבְכֶם אַל תִּירְאוּ וְאַל תַּחְפְּזוּ וְגוֹ׳״. ״אַל יֵרַךְ לְבַבְכֶם״ — מִפְּנֵי צׇהֳלַת סוּסִים וְצִחְצוּחַ חֲרָבוֹת, ״אַל תִּירְאוּ״ — מִפְּנֵי הַגָּפַת תְּרִיסִין וְשִׁפְעַת הַקַּלְגַּסִּין, ״אַל תַּחְפְּזוּ״ — מִקּוֹל קְרָנוֹת, ״אַל תַּעַרְצוּ״ — מִפְּנֵי קוֹל צְווֹחוֹת.", "context": "Read segments 8,9,10,11,12 of Sotah 42a. Embedded Mishnah explains do not lose heart as horse neighing and sword clashes; adjacent divine aid exhortation does not make the horses supernatural.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Embedded Mishnah explains do not lose heart as horse neighing and sword clashes; adjacent divine aid exhortation does not make the horses supernatural.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "battle_noise_exhortation", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-yevamot-90b-10-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Yevamot", "locator": "90b:10", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Yevamot.90b.10", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Yevamot.90b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תָּא שְׁמַע, אָמַר רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב: שָׁמַעְתִּי שֶׁבֵּית דִּין מַכִּין וְעוֹנְשִׁין שֶׁלֹּא מִן הַתּוֹרָה, וְלֹא לַעֲבוֹר עַל דִּבְרֵי תוֹרָה, אֶלָּא לַעֲשׂוֹת סְיָיג לַתּוֹרָה. וּמַעֲשֶׂה בְּאָדָם אֶחָד שֶׁרָכַב עַל סוּס בַּשַּׁבָּת בִּימֵי יְוָנִים — וֶהֱבִיאוּהוּ לְבֵית דִּין וּסְקָלוּהוּ, לֹא מִפְּנֵי שֶׁרָאוּי לְכָךְ, אֶלָּא שֶׁהַשָּׁעָה צְרִיכָה לְכָךְ.", "context": "Read segments 8,9,10,11,12 of Yevamot 90b. R. Eliezer ben Jacob’s same Sabbath horse rider punishment exemplum in discussion of rabbinic powers; separate canonical parallel to Sanhedrin 46a, not another historically verified event.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Eliezer ben Jacob’s same Sabbath horse rider punishment exemplum in discussion of rabbinic powers; separate canonical parallel to Sanhedrin 46a, not another historically verified event.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "emergency_sabbath_punishment_parallel", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-yoma-69a-13-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Yoma", "locator": "69a:13", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma.69a.13", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Yoma.69a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מִיָּד נְקָבוּם בְּעִקְבֵיהֶם וּתְלָאוּם בְּזַנְבֵי סוּסֵיהֶם, וְהָיוּ מְגָרְרִין אוֹתָן עַל הַקּוֹצִים וְעַל הַבַּרְקָנִים, עַד שֶׁהִגִּיעוּ לְהַר גְּרִיזִים. כֵּיוָן שֶׁהִגִּיעוּ לְהַר גְּרִיזִים — חֲרָשׁוּהוּ, וּזְרָעוּהוּ כַּרְשִׁינִין, כְּדֶרֶךְ שֶׁבִּקְּשׁוּ לַעֲשׂוֹת לְבֵית אֱלֹהֵינוּ. וְאוֹתוֹ הַיּוֹם עֲשָׂאוּהוּ יוֹם טוֹב.", "context": "Read segments 11,12,13,14,15 of Yoma 69a. Narrative after Alexander meets Simeon the Just: opponents are attached to horse tails and dragged to Gerizim. Adjacent visionary likeness motivates Alexander, not extraordinary properties of horses.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Narrative after Alexander meets Simeon the Just: opponents are attached to horse tails and dragged to Gerizim. Adjacent visionary likeness motivates Alexander, not extraordinary properties of horses.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-004", "role": "punitive_dragging", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-avodah-zarah-1-6-1-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Avodah Zarah", "locator": "1:6:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Avodah_Zarah.1.6.1", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "משנה: מְקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ לִמְכּוֹר בְּהֵמָה דַקָּה לַגּוֹיִם מוֹכְרִין. מְקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ שֶׁלֹּא לִמְכּוֹר אֵין מוֹכְרִין וְאַל יְשַׁנֶּה אָדָם מִפְּנֵי הָמַּחֲלוֹקֶת. וּבְכָל מָקוֹם אֵין מוֹכְרִין לָהֶם בְּהֵמָה גַסָּה עֲגָלִים וּסְיָיחִים שְׁלֵמִין וּשְׁבוּרִין. רִבִּי יְהוּדָה מַתִּיר בַּשְּׁבוּרָה בֶּן בְּתֵירָא מַתִּיר בַּסּוּס:", "context": "Embedded Mishnah lists restrictions on large-animal sales and Ben Beteira’s horse exception; complete Mishnah segment read.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Embedded Mishnah lists restrictions on large-animal sales and Ben Beteira’s horse exception; complete Mishnah segment read.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "YER-004", "categories": ["halakha", "horse_sale"], "role": "horse_sale", "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "quote_format": "Previously downloaded YER-002 full original Hebrew segment read; copied exactly with edition pointing/brackets; no fresh manuscript collation.", "limitations": ["Reviewed saved primary digital segment, not freshly retrieved entire halakha.", "Context limited to complete segment unless additional segment explicitly named.", "Commentaries and manuscript variants not collated; independent review not performed."], "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Nezikin/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20A