{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-pesachim-4-3-1-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Pesachim", "locator": "4:3:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Pesachim.4.3.1", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "משנה: מְקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ לִמְכּוֹר בְּהֵמָה דַקָּה לַגּוֹיִם מוֹכְרִין. מְקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ שֶׁלֹּא לִמְכּוֹר אֵין מוֹכְרִין. וְאַל יְשַׁנֶּה אָדָם מִפְּנֵי הַמַּחֲלוֹקֶת. וּבְכָל מָקוֹם אֵין מוֹכְרִין לָהֶן בְּהֵמָה גַסָּה עֲגָלִים וּסְיָיחִים שְׁלֵימִין וּשְׁבוּרִין. רִבִּי יְהוּדָה מַתִּיר בַּשְּׁבוּרָה. בֶּן בְּתֵירָה מַתִּיר בַּסּוּס:", "context": "Complete embedded Mishnah read; local sale custom, large-animal restriction, R. Judah’s broken-animal and Ben Beteira’s horse exceptions. Parallel wording at Avodah Zarah 1:6:1 is retained as distinct canonical occurrence.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete embedded Mishnah read; local sale custom, large-animal restriction, R. Judah’s broken-animal and Ben Beteira’s horse exceptions. Parallel wording at Avodah Zarah 1:6:1 is retained as distinct canonical occurrence.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["BAV-003-YER-004-worker"], "task_id": "YER-004", "categories": ["halakha", "horse_sale"], "role": "horse_sale", "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "quote_format": "Previously downloaded YER-002 full original Hebrew segment read; copied exactly with edition pointing/brackets; no fresh manuscript collation.", "limitations": ["Reviewed saved primary digital segment, not freshly retrieved entire halakha.", "Context limited to complete segment unless additional segment explicitly named.", "Commentaries and manu