{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-pesachim-53a-11-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Pesachim", "locator": "53a:11", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim.53a.11", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Pesachim.53a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַתְנִי׳ מָקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ לִמְכּוֹר בְּהֵמָה דַּקָּה לַגּוֹיִם — מוֹכְרִין, מָקוֹם שֶׁלֹּא נָהֲגוּ לִמְכּוֹר — אֵין מוֹכְרִין. וּבְכׇל מָקוֹם אֵין מוֹכְרִין לָהֶם בְּהֵמָה גַּסָּה, עֲגָלִים וּסְיָיחִין, שְׁלֵמִין וּשְׁבוּרִין. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה מַתִּיר בַּשְּׁבוּרָה. בֶּן בְּתִירָא מַתִּיר בַּסּוּס.", "context": "Read segments 9,10,11,12,13 of Pesachim 53a. Embedded Mishnah prohibits large-animal sales to gentiles and records Ben Beteira’s horse exception; separate canonical occurrence of shared Mishnah.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Embedded Mishnah prohibits large-animal sales to gentiles and records Ben Beteira’s horse exception; separate canonical occurrence of shared Mishnah.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_sale_mishnah", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-pesachim-94a-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Pesachim", "locator": "94a:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim.94a.2", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Pesachim.94a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: הָיָה עוֹמֵד חוּץ לַמּוֹדִיעִים, וְיָכוֹל לִיכָּנֵס בְּסוּסִים וּבִפְרָדִים, יָכוֹל יְהֵא חַיָּיב — תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר: ״וּבְדֶרֶךְ לֹא הָיָה״, וְהַלָּה הָיָה בַּדֶּרֶךְ.", "context": "Read segments 1,2,3,4 of Pesachim 94a. A person beyond Modiim remains exempt as distant even if horses or mules could bring him to Passover sacrifice; adjacent case contrasts traffic obstruction within boundary.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A person beyond Modiim remains exempt as distant even if horses or mules could bring him to Passover sacrifice; adjacent case contrasts traffic obstruction within boundary.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "passover_travel_mount", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-26b-1-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "26b:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.26b.1", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.26b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אֲמַרוּ לֵיהּ: מַשְׁירְיָיתָךְ הֵיכָא? אֲמַר: הֲדַרוּ בִּי. אֲמַרוּ לֵיהּ: אִם כֵּן, אַחוֹכֵי קָא מַחְיְיכַתְּ בַּן! נְקָבוּהוּ בַּעֲקָבָיו וּתְלָאוּהוּ בְּזַנְבֵי סוּסֵיהֶם, וְהָיוּ מְגָרְרִין אוֹתוֹ עַל הַקּוֹצִים וְעַל הַבַּרְקָנִין.", "context": "Read segments 1,2,3 of Sanhedrin 26b. Continuation of Shebna narrative: Assyrians ask where his camp is; on learning followers abandoned him they attach him to horse tails and drag him on thorns. Horses are punitive transport, not supernatural beings. Also read preceding 26a:24–27: Shebna’s grave dishonor and Gabriel closing door against followers; miracle affects access, not horse nature.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Continuation of Shebna narrative: Assyrians ask where his camp is; on learning followers abandoned him they attach him to horse tails and drag him on thorns. Horses are punitive transport, not supernatural beings.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "shebna_punitive_dragging", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-63b-17-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "63b:17", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.63b.17", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.63b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "״וְהַסְפַרְוִים שֹׂרְפִים אֶת בְּנֵיהֶם וְאֶת בְּנוֹתֵיהֶם בָּאֵשׁ לְאַדְרַמֶּלֶךְ וַעֲנַמֶּלֶךְ אֱלֹהֵי סְפַרְוָיִם״, וּמַאי נִיהוּ? הַפֶּרֶד וְהַסּוּס. אַדְרַמֶּלֶךְ – דְּאָדַר לֵיהּ לְמָרֵיהּ בִּטְעִינָה, וַעֲנַמֶּלֶךְ – דְּעָנֵי לֵיהּ לְמָרֵיהּ בִּקְרָבָא.", "context": "Read segments 15,16,17,18,19 of Sanhedrin 63b. Exegetical identification of Sepharvaim’s Adrammelech and Anammelech as mule and horse, explained by load bearing and battle assistance. This is a rabbinic interpretation of foreign cult names, not independently verified cult history or actual divine horses. Requires independent review for central spiritual conclusions.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Exegetical identification of Sepharvaim’s Adrammelech and Anammelech as mule and horse, explained by load bearing and battle assistance. This is a rabbinic interpretation of foreign cult names, not independently verified cult history or actual divine horses. Requires independent review for central spiritual conclusions.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_idol_exegesis", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-94b-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "94b:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.94b.2", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.94b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "פַּרְעֹה, דִּכְתִיב בֵּיהּ: ״מִי ה׳ אֲשֶׁר אֶשְׁמַע בְּקֹלוֹ״, נִפְרַע הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא מִמֶּנּוּ בְּעַצְמוֹ, דִּכְתִיב: ״וַיְנַעֵר ה׳ אֶת מִצְרַיִם בְּתוֹךְ הַיָּם״, וּכְתִיב: ״דָּרַכְתָּ בַּיָּם סוּסֶיךָ וְגוֹ׳״. סַנְחֵרִיב, דִּכְתִיב: ״בְּיַד מַלְאָכֶיךָ חֵרַפְתָּ ה׳״, נִפְרַע הַקָּדוֹשׁ בָּרוּךְ הוּא מִמֶּנּוּ עַל יְדֵי שָׁלִיחַ, דִּכְתִיב: ״וַיֵּצֵא מַלְאַךְ ה׳ וַיַּךְ בְּמַחֲנֵה אַשּׁוּר מֵאָה שְׁמוֹנִים וַחֲמִשָּׁה אֶלֶף וְגוֹ׳״.", "context": "Read segments 1,2,3,4 of Sanhedrin 94b. Habakkuk’s Thou didst tread the sea with Thy horses is cited to show God personally punished Pharaoh, unlike Sennacherib punished through an angel. Explicit divine-horse biblical imagery used in exegesis; no taxonomy of literal celestial horses established. Requires independent review for central interpretation.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Habakkuk’s Thou didst tread the sea with Thy horses is cited to show God personally punished Pharaoh, unlike Sennacherib punished through an angel. Explicit divine-horse biblical imagery used in exegesis; no taxonomy of literal celestial horses established. Requires independent review for central interpretation.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "divine_horses_biblical_theophany", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-95b-6-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "95b:6", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.95b.6", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.95b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "בְּמַתְנִיתָא תָּנָא: אוֹרֶךְ מַחֲנֵהוּ אַרְבַּע מֵאוֹת פַּרְסָה, רֹחַב צַוַּאר סוּסָיו אַרְבָּעִים פַּרְסָה. סַךְ מַחֲנֵהוּ מָאתַיִם וְשִׁשִּׁים רִיבּוֹא אֲלָפִים חָסֵר חַד. בָּעֵי אַבָּיֵי: חָסֵר חַד רִיבּוֹיָא, אוֹ חָסַר חַד אַלְפָּא, אוֹ חָסַר מְאָה, אוֹ חָסַר חַד? תֵּיקוּ.", "context": "Read segments 4,5,6,7,8 of Sanhedrin 95b. A baraita gives enormous dimensions of Sennacherib’s camp and forty parasangs for the breadth of his horses’ necks; preceding account lists cavalry and parallels future Gog army. Aggadic scale/hyperbole, not proven giant horse anatomy or military census.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "A baraita gives enormous dimensions of Sennacherib’s camp and forty parasangs for the breadth of his horses’ necks; preceding account lists cavalry and parallels future Gog army. Aggadic scale/hyperbole, not proven giant horse anatomy or military census.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "sennacherib_army_hyperbole", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-98b-1-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "98b:1", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.98b.1", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.98b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "שֶׁאֵין כׇּל דֶּקֶל וָדֶקֶל שֶׁבְּבָבֶל, שֶׁאֵין סוּס שֶׁל פָּרְסִיִּים נִקְשָׁר בּוֹ, וְאֵין לָךְ כׇּל אָרוֹן וְאָרוֹן שֶׁבְּאֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל, שֶׁאֵין סוּס מָדִי אוֹכֵל בּוֹ תֶּבֶן.", "context": "Also read 98a:18–21, establishing R. Yose ben Kisma’s attribution and deathbed coffin instruction. Continuation of R. Yose ben Kisma’s deathbed instruction to deepen his coffin: Persian horses tied to Babylonian palms and Median horses feeding in Land of Israel coffins portray foreign occupation and grave desecration. Preceding predicted redemption and blood-water sign are separate; horses remain occupation animals, not celestial.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Continuation of R. Yose ben Kisma’s deathbed instruction to deepen his coffin: Persian horses tied to Babylonian palms and Median horses feeding in Land of Israel coffins portray foreign occupation and grave desecration. Preceding predicted redemption and blood-water sign are separate; horses remain occupation animals, not celestial.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "premessianic_occupation", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-98b-11-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "98b:11", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.98b.11", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.98b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר רַב פָּפָּא: הַיְינוּ דְּאָמְרִי אִינָשֵׁי, רָהֵיט וְנָפֵל תּוֹרָא, וְאָזֵיל וְשָׁדֵי לֵיהּ סוּסְיָא בְּאוּרְיֵיהּ.", "context": "Read segments 9,10,11,12,13 of Sanhedrin 98b. Rav Pappa cites proverb of an ox running/falling and a horse put into its manger, following divine hesitation over destroying one people for another. Horse/ox substitution is an analogy within redemption discussion, not supernatural zoology.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Rav Pappa cites proverb of an ox running/falling and a horse put into its manger, following divine hesitation over destroying one people for another. Horse/ox substitution is an analogy within redemption discussion, not supernatural zoology.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "bull_horse_manger_proverb", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-105a-16-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "105a:16", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.105a.16", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.105a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: בִּלְעָם חִיגֵּר בְּרַגְלוֹ אַחַת הָיָה, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״וַיֵּלֶךְ שֶׁפִי״. שִׁמְשׁוֹן בִּשְׁתֵּי רַגְלָיו, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״שְׁפִיפֹן עֲלֵי אֹרַח הַנּוֹשֵׁךְ עִקְּבֵי סוּס״. בִּלְעָם סוֹמֵא בְּאַחַת מֵעֵינָיו הָיָה, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״שְׁתֻם הָעָיִן״.", "context": "Read segments 14,15,16,17 of Sanhedrin 105a. R. Yohanan infers Samson’s disability from serpent biting horse heels in Genesis 49:17, alongside Balaam disability interpretations. Horse is part of cited scriptural simile.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Yohanan infers Samson’s disability from serpent biting horse heels in Genesis 49:17, alongside Balaam disability interpretations. Horse is part of cited scriptural simile.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "samson_scriptural_horse_simile", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-sanhedrin-105b-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Sanhedrin", "locator": "105b:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin.105b.2", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Sanhedrin.105b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "״וְיֹדֵעַ דַּעַת עֶלְיוֹן״. הַשְׁתָּא דַּעַת בְּהֶמְתּוֹ לָא הֲוָה יָדַע, דַּעַת עֶלְיוֹן הֲוָה יָדַע? מַאי דַּעַת בְּהֶמְתּוֹ? דְּאָמְרִי לֵיהּ: מַאי טַעְמָא לָא רָכְבַתְּ סוּסְיָא? אֲמַר לְהוּ: שְׁדַאי לֵהּוֹ בִּרְטִיבָא.", "context": "Read segments 1,2,3,4 of Sanhedrin 105b. Balaam asked why he does not ride a horse claims he put it in pasture; next segments present speaking donkey rebuttal. Supernatural speech belongs to donkey, not absent horse.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Balaam asked why he does not ride a horse claims he put it in pasture; next segments present speaking donkey rebuttal. Supernatural speech belongs to donkey, not absent horse.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "balaam_excuse_missing_horse", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-avodah-zarah-4b-2-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Avodah Zarah", "locator": "4b:2", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah.4b.2", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Avodah_Zarah.4b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַאי ״דַּעַת בְּהֶמְתּוֹ לָא הֲוָה יָדַע״? בְּעִידָּנָא דַּחֲזוֹ לֵיהּ דַּהֲוָה רְכִיב אַחֲמָרֵיהּ, אֲמַרוּ לֵיהּ: מַאי טַעְמָא לָא רְכַבְתָּא אַסּוּסְיָא? אֲמַר לְהוּ: בִּרְטִיבָא שְׁדַאי לֵיהּ. מִיָּד: ״וַתֹּאמֶר הָאָתוֹן הֲלֹא אָנֹכִי אֲתֹנְךָ״, אֲמַר לַהּ: לִטְעִינָא בְּעָלְמָא.", "context": "Read segments 1,2,3,4 of Avodah Zarah 4b. Balaam seen on donkey is asked why he has not ridden horse; claims horse is grazing. Donkey immediately speaks. Parallel to Sanhedrin 105b; horse is proposed ordinary mount, not speaking animal.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Balaam seen on donkey is asked why he has not ridden horse; claims horse is grazing. Donkey immediately speaks. Parallel to Sanhedrin 105b; horse is proposed ordinary mount, not speaking animal.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "balaam_excuse_parallel", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-avodah-zarah-7b-9-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Avodah Zarah", "locator": "7b:9", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah.7b.9", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Avodah_Zarah.7b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תַּנְיָא אִידַּךְ: נַחוּם הַמָּדִי אוֹמֵר: מוֹכְרִין לָהֶן סוּס זָכָר וְזָקֵן בַּמִּלְחָמָה. אָמְרוּ לוֹ: נִשְׁתַּקַּע הַדָּבָר וְלֹא נֶאֱמַר.", "context": "Read segments 7,8,9,10,11 of Avodah Zarah 7b. Nahum the Mede permits sale of male aged horse for battle; other sages reject his statement. Attributed legal dispute, not general permission or independently verified military practice.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Nahum the Mede permits sale of male aged horse for battle; other sages reject his statement. Attributed legal dispute, not general permission or independently verified military practice.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_sale_disputed_opinion", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-avodah-zarah-7b-10-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Avodah Zarah", "locator": "7b:10", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah.7b.10", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Avodah_Zarah.7b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "וְהָאִיכָּא בֶּן בְּתִירָא דְּקָאֵי כְּוָותֵיהּ, דִּתְנַן: בֶּן בְּתִירָא מַתִּיר בַּסּוּס. בֶּן בְּתִירָא לָא מְפַלֵּיג בֵּין זְכָרִים לִנְקֵבוֹת, אִיהוּ מִדְּקָא מְפַלֵּיג בֵּין זְכָרִים לִנְקֵבוֹת, כְּרַבָּנַן סְבִירָא לֵיהּ. וּלְרַבָּנַן נִשְׁתַּקַּע הַדָּבָר וְלֹא נֶאֱמַר.", "context": "Read segments 8,9,10,11,12 of Avodah Zarah 7b. Discussion rejects assimilation of Nahum’s gender-limited permission to Ben Beteira’s unrestricted horse exception; separate segment within same sale dispute.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Discussion rejects assimilation of Nahum’s gender-limited permission to Ben Beteira’s unrestricted horse exception; separate segment within same sale dispute.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_sale_gender_distinction", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-avodah-zarah-14b-9-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Avodah Zarah", "locator": "14b:9", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah.14b.9", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Avodah_Zarah.14b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַתְנִי׳ מָקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ לִמְכּוֹר בְּהֵמָה דַּקָּה לַגּוֹיִם — מוֹכְרִין, מָקוֹם שֶׁנָּהֲגוּ שֶׁלֹּא לִמְכּוֹר — אֵין מוֹכְרִין. וּבְכׇל מָקוֹם אֵין מוֹכְרִין לָהֶם בְּהֵמָה גַּסָּה, עֲגָלִים וּסְיָיחִים, שְׁלֵמִין ושְׁבוּרִין. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה מַתִּיר בַּשְּׁבוּרָה, וּבֶן בְּתִירָא מַתִּיר בַּסּוּס.", "context": "Read segments 7,8,9,10,11 of Avodah Zarah 14b. Embedded Mishnah on gentile animal sales repeats Ben Beteira’s horse exception; adjacent sugya concerns local custom and sale/seclusion. Canonical parallel to Pesachim 53a.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Embedded Mishnah on gentile animal sales repeats Ben Beteira’s horse exception; adjacent sugya concerns local custom and sale/seclusion. Canonical parallel to Pesachim 53a.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_sale_mishnah_parallel", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bava-kamma-37a-26-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bava Kamma", "locator": "37a:26", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Kamma.37a.26", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bava_Kamma.37a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: רָאָה שׁוֹר – נָגַח, חֲמוֹר – לֹא נָגַח, סוּס – נָגַח, גָּמָל – לֹא נָגַח, פֶּרֶד – נָגַח, עָרוֹד – לֹא נָגַח; נַעֲשָׂה מוּעָד לְסֵירוּגִין לַכֹּל.", "context": "Read segments 24,25,26,27 of Bava Kamma 37a. Baraita treats alternating goring of ox, horse and mule, with donkey/camel/wild ass not gored, as recurrent alternate liability pattern for all animals. Horse is hypothetical damage victim.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Baraita treats alternating goring of ox, horse and mule, with donkey/camel/wild ass not gored, as recurrent alternate liability pattern for all animals. Horse is hypothetical damage victim.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "goring_species_sequence", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bava-metzia-108a-8-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bava Metzia", "locator": "108a:8", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Metzia.108a.8", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bava_Metzia.108a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: הַאי מַאן דְּאַחְזֵיק בְּרַקְתָּא דְנַהְרָא – חֲצִיפָא הָוֵי, סַלּוֹקֵי לָא מְסַלְּקִינַן לֵיהּ. וְהָאִידָּנָא דְּקָא כָּתְבִי פָּרְסָאֵי: קְנֵי לָךְ עַד מְלֵי צַוְּארֵי סוּסְיָא מַיָּא – סַלּוֹקֵי נָמֵי מְסַלְּקִינַן לֵיהּ.", "context": "Read segments 6,7,8,9,10 of Bava Metzia 108a. Shmuel discusses occupation of riverbank; Persian deeds’ wording about horse-neck-depth water changes removal rule. Horse is measure/reference in waterway rights; exact practice not independently established.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Shmuel discusses occupation of riverbank; Persian deeds’ wording about horse-neck-depth water changes removal rule. Horse is measure/reference in waterway rights; exact practice not independently established.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "riverbank_horse_towing_boundary", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-2a-7-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "2a:7", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.2a.7", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.2a?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "תְּנַן הָתָם: רַבִּי יְהוּדָה מַתִּיר בַּשְּׁבוּרָה, בֶּן בְּתִירָא מַתִּיר בַּסּוּס.", "context": "Read segments 5,6,7,8,9 of Bekhorot 2a. Horse sale permission of Ben Beteira quoted with R. Judah’s disabled-animal permission; next discussion applies latter to embryos. Horse belongs to cited legal comparison.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Horse sale permission of Ben Beteira quoted with R. Judah’s disabled-animal permission; next discussion applies latter to embryos. Horse belongs to cited legal comparison.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_sale_cited_mishnah", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-5b-3-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "5b:3", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.5b.3", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.5b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "אָמַר רַבִּי חֲנִינָא: שָׁאַלְתִּי אֶת רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בְּבֵית מוֹתְבָא רַבָּא, מָה נִשְׁתַּנּוּ פִּטְרֵי חֲמוֹרִים מִפִּטְרֵי סוּסִים וּגְמַלִּים? אָמַר לִי: גְּזֵירַת הַכָּתוּב הִיא, וְעוֹד שֶׁסִּיְּיעוּ יִשְׂרָאֵל בִּשְׁעַת יְצִיאָתָם מִמִּצְרַיִם, שֶׁאֵין לָךְ כׇּל אֶחָד וְאֶחָד מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁלֹּא הָיוּ עִמּוֹ תִּשְׁעִים חֲמוֹרִים לוּבִים טְעוּנִים מִכַּסְפָּהּ וּזְהָבָהּ שֶׁל מִצְרַיִם.", "context": "Read segments 1,2,3,4,5 of Bekhorot 5b. R. Hanina asks R. Eliezer why donkey firstborn differ from horses and camels; answer Scripture’s decree and donkeys’ service carrying Egypt wealth. Horses serve species contrast; ninety laden donkeys per Israelite is attributed aggadah, not census.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Hanina asks R. Eliezer why donkey firstborn differ from horses and camels; answer Scripture’s decree and donkeys’ service carrying Egypt wealth. Horses serve species contrast; ninety laden donkeys per Israelite is attributed aggadah, not census.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "firstborn_species_exclusion_reason", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-5b-7-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "5b:7", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.5b.7", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.5b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מַתְנִי׳ פָּרָה שֶׁיָּלְדָה מִין חֲמוֹר, וַחֲמוֹר שֶׁיָּלְדָה כְּמִין סוּס — פְּטוּרָה מִן הַבְּכוֹרָה, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״פֶּטֶר חֲמוֹר״ ״פֶּטֶר חֲמוֹר״ שְׁנֵי פְּעָמִים, עַד שֶׁיְּהֵא הַיּוֹלֵד חֲמוֹר וְהַנּוֹלָד חֲמוֹר.", "context": "Read segments 5,6,7,8,9 of Bekhorot 5b. Embedded Mishnah exempts donkey bearing horse-like offspring from firstborn rule, requiring donkey parent and donkey offspring. Legal classification of appearance, not evidence of a miraculous cross-species birth.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Embedded Mishnah exempts donkey bearing horse-like offspring from firstborn rule, requiring donkey parent and donkey offspring. Legal classification of appearance, not evidence of a miraculous cross-species birth.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_like_offspring_hypothetical", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "bavli-bekhorot-5b-28-davidson", "corpus_id": "bavli", "work": "Bekhorot", "locator": "5b:28", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.5b.28", "access_url": "https://www.sefaria.org/api/texts/Bekhorot.5b?context=0&commentary=0", "edition": "William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "מִיבְּעֵי לֵיהּ לְכִדְתַנְיָא: רַבִּי יוֹסֵי הַגְּלִילִי אוֹמֵר, מִתּוֹךְ שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר ״אַךְ פָּדֹה תִפְדֶּה אֶת בְּכוֹר הָאָדָם וְאֵת בְּכוֹר הַבְּהֵמָה הַטְּמֵאָה תִּפְדֶּה״, שׁוֹמֵעַ אֲנִי אֲפִילּוּ פִּטְרֵי סוּסִים וּגְמַלִּים? תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר ״פֶּטֶר חֲמוֹר״ — פֶּטֶר חֲמוֹר אָמַרְתִּי לְךָ, וְלֹא פִּטְרֵי סוּסִים וּגְמַלִּים.", "context": "Read segments 26,27,28,29 of Bekhorot 5b. R. Yose the Galilean’s exposition considers and excludes horse/camel firstborn from donkey redemption command; following challenge tests whether other redemption medium remains, continuation rejects using repeated donkey wording. Legal hermeneutic, not horse sanctity claim. Also read 6a:1–5 continuation; repeated donkey wording excludes horse/camel firstborn. These additional segments are context-only, not new accepted ledger entries.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "R. Yose the Galilean’s exposition considers and excludes horse/camel firstborn from donkey redemption command; following challenge tests whether other redemption medium remains, continuation rejects using repeated donkey wording. Legal hermeneutic, not horse sanctity claim.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "BAV-005", "role": "horse_firstborn_redemption_exclusion", "limitations": ["Digital API edition; no manuscripts/traditional commentaries or independent review.", "Narrative/legal testimony is not independent historical or zoological verification."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-bava-batra-8-4-4-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Bava Batra", "locator": "8:4:4", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Bava_Batra.8.4.4", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Nezikin/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Bava%20Batra/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "שְׁמוּאֵל שָׁאַל לְרַב הוּנָא. מַתָּנָה שֶׁכָּתַב בִּלְשׁוֹן מֶכֶר מָהוּ. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. אַרְכְּבֵיהּ אַתְּרֵי רִיכְשֵׁי בַּרְקֵי. אָמַר רִבִּי חִזְקִיָּה. לָא אָמְרֵי אֶלָּא מַיְיתוּ תְּרֵין סוּסְוָון חִיוְורִין וּמַרְכִּיבִין עַל תְּרֵיהוֹן וְדֵין אָזְלָא בְּדָא וְדֵין אָזְלָא בְּדָא וּמִשְׁתַּכַּח לָא צַיַיד כְּלוּם.", "context": "Complete segment: Shmuel asks Rav Huna about a gift written as sale. Riding two white horses moving in different directions illustrates conflicting legal forms and gaining nothing; R. Hezekiah’s simile, not celestial horses.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment: Shmuel asks Rav Huna about a gift written as sale. Riding two white horses moving in different directions illustrates conflicting legal forms and gaining nothing; R. Hezekiah’s simile, not celestial horses.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "YER-006", "role": "two_horse_legal_simile", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
{"schema_version": 1, "id": "yerushalmi-kiddushin-1-5-8-guggenheimer", "corpus_id": "yerushalmi", "work": "Jerusalem Talmud Kiddushin", "locator": "1:5:8", "url": "https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Kiddushin.1.5.8", "access_url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/sefaria-export/json/Talmud/Yerushalmi/Seder%20Nashim/Jerusalem%20Talmud%20Kiddushin/Hebrew/merged.json", "edition": "The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015", "language": "Hebrew/Aramaic", "mention_type": "direct", "parent_source_id": null, "quote": "בְּכֶסֶף. רִבִּי בָּא סְבַר מֵימַר. בְּכֶסֶף עַל מְנָת שֶׁלֹּא יִכְתּוֹב אוֹנֵי. אֲבָל בְּכֶסֶף עַל מְנָת לִכְתוֹב לוֹ אוֹנֵי לֹא קָנָה עַד שָׁעָה שֶׁיִּכְתּוֹב אוֹנֵי. רִבִּי יוֹנָה וְרִבִּי יוֹסֵי פְלִיגִין. אַתְיָיא דְּרִבִּי בָּא כִּשְׁמוּאֵל וּדְרַב הוּנָא כְּרִבִּי יוֹחָנָן. דְּרִבִּי בָּא כִּשְׁמוּאֵל. שְׁמוּאֵל שָׁאַל לְרַב חוּנָה. שׁוֹחֵט וְנִתְעַסֵּק בַּקֳּדָשִׁים. אָמַר לֵיהּ. לִרְצוֹנְכֶם. פְּרָט לְמִתְעַסֵּק. כָּתַב מַתָּנָה בִּלְשׁוֹן קִנְיָין. אֲמַר לֵיהּ. אַרְכְּבֵיהּ אַתְּרֵי רִיכְשֵׁי. אָמְרָהּ רִבִּי בָּא וְלֹא קִיבְּלָהּ שְׁמוּאֵל. מָהוּ אַרְכְּבֵיהּ עַל תְּרֵין רִיכְשֵׁי בַּרְקֵי. סָבְרִין מֵימַר. מַיְיתֵי תְּרֵין סוּסְוָון שַׁטְיֵי וּמְרַכְּבִין לֵיהּ עַל תְּרֵיהוֹן וְהַהוּא אֲזִיל בְּדָא וְהַהֵין אֲזַל בְּדָא לֹא אַשְׁכָּח גַּבֵּי כְּלוּם. אָמַר רִבִּי יוֹסֵי מַמְלְחָיָיא. יִיפֶּה כוֹחוֹ בִּשְׁנֵי דְבָרִים. שֶׁיֵּשׁ שִׁיעְבּוּד לִמְכִירָה וְאֵין שִׁיעְבּוּד לְמַתָּנָה. שֶׁהַמּוֹכֵר לֹא מָכַר אֶת הַכֹּל וְהַנּוֹתֵן מַתָּנָה נָתַן אֶת הַכֹּל. וּדְרַב חוּנָה כְּרִבִּי יוֹחָנָן. חַד בַּר נַשׁ מִי דְמִיךְ אָמַר. יִנָּתְנוּ כָּל נְכָסַיי לִפְלוֹנִי. חָזַר וְאָמַר. כִּתְבוּ וּתְנוּ. רִבִּי לָעְזָר וְרִבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בַּר יָקִים אַעֲלוֹן עוֹבְדָא קוֹמֵי רִבִּי יוֹחָנָן. אָמַר. אִם אָמַר. לִזְכוּתוֹ. דִּבְרֵי הַכֹּל זָכָה. וְאִם לְזַכּוֹתוֹ בִּכְתָב. כָּל עַמָּא מוֹדֵיי שֶׁאֵין אָדָם זוֹכֶה בִּכְתָב לְאַחַר מִיתָה. מִי מוֹדִיעַ. אֶת רְבוּ. תִּיפְתָּר שֶׁהָיוּ שָׁם עֵדִים יוֹדְעִים. הַגַּע עַצְמָךְ שֶׁאֵין שָׁם עֵדִים יוֹדְעִין. אָמַר רִבִּי יוֹסֵי. לְעוֹלָם הַשָּׂדֶה בְחֶזְקַת בְּעָלֶיהָ וּמוֹצִיא מֵחֲבֵירוֹ עָלָיו הָרְאָיָיה.", "context": "Complete segment discusses acquisition with money/document and gift written as sale. Two foolish horses going different ways explains a contested reading of riding two mounts; R. Yose offers instead strengthened rights in two respects. Legal metaphor and disagreement, not supernatural horse narrative.", "checks": {"primary_read": true, "quote_verified": true, "context_checked": true, "attribution_verified": true, "commentaries_checked": false, "interpretation_prepared": true, "independent_reviewed": false}, "interpretation": "Complete segment discusses acquisition with money/document and gift written as sale. Two foolish horses going different ways explains a contested reading of riding two mounts; R. Yose offers instead strengthened rights in two respects. Legal metaphor and disagreement, not supernatural horse narrative.", "epistemic_type": "primary_text", "reviewers": ["talmud-finish-worker"], "task_id": "YER-006", "role": "two_horse_legal_simile_parallel", "limitations": ["Complete saved YER-002 export-derived primary segment read; no fresh surrounding halakha retrieved.", "Merged export provenance not manuscript collation; no traditional commentaries or independent review."], "accessed_at": "2026-10-10", "period_status": "Historical composition/edition dating not independently established", "confidence": {"quotation": "verified_in_named_digital_witness", "interpretation": "working_contextual_reading"}}
